{
  "$schema": "https://appflare.github.io/catalog/schema/v1.json",
  "slug": "shotsync",
  "name": "ShotSync",
  "summary": "A private image and text pool shared across your devices: drop a screenshot or snippet on one, grab it on another, from an installable web app backed by R2.",
  "tagline": "Share pictures and text between your devices, privately",
  "features": [
    "Upload photos, screenshots, and text snippets to a shared device gallery",
    "Copy text or download images on another device",
    "Share one item with a public link that expires after seven days",
    "Add the gallery to your phone's home screen",
    "Delete several items at once"
  ],
  "repo": "Defiabell/shotsync",
  "homepage": "https://shotsync-demo.defiabell.workers.dev",
  "license": "MIT",
  "categories": ["files", "sharing"],
  // The formatting of URLs in the notes changed after this release was published:
  // a revision, no new build.
  // Display features (revision 4).
  "revision": 4,
  "authors": [{ "name": "Jinkun Sun", "github": "Defiabell" }],
  "maintainers": ["MendyLanda"],
  // The newest release tag. The commits after it add upstream's hosted,
  // multi-account variant (its own config, wrangler.hosted.jsonc, with D1);
  // the self-hosted Worker installed here is the one in wrangler.toml.
  "source": { "ref": "v1.0.0", "sha": "39c024a4d93095b5cddfbe4ad9950a37d7e319a4" },
  "install": {
    "packageManager": "npm",
    // The top-level Worker. The `demo` environment in the same file is
    // upstream's read-only public demo and is not installed.
    "wranglerConfig": "wrangler.toml"
  },
  // One Worker and one R2 bucket (10 GB free); the Worker does no image
  // processing, since the browser converts and thumbnails before uploading.
  "plan": "free",
  "requires": ["r2"],
  "secrets": [
    {
      "name": "AUTH_TOKEN",
      "label": "Access token",
      "help": "The one shared secret for the pool: every device enters it once, and it also signs the 7-day share links, so changing it invalidates links already shared. Copy it now.",
      "generate": "password"
    }
  ],
  "postInstall": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "Open {{appUrl}} on each device and enter the access token once; it is kept in that browser. On a phone, add the page to the home screen to use it like an app. The interface is in Chinese; upstream's README maps each button to English."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "Upstream keeps items for 30 days with an R2 lifecycle rule, which Appflare does not create. To get the same, open the app's R2 bucket in the Cloudflare dashboard and add an object lifecycle rule under Settings that deletes objects 30 days after upload."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "Upstream also has a Mac menu-bar app that uploads every screenshot, and an iOS Shortcut for the share sheet (`mac/` and `shortcut/` in the repository); point them at `{{appUrl}}` with the same token."
    }
  ]
}
